        "original_id": "6ca82f14-870f-5f53-9c48-fe6ecef57ad5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shane Meadows\n- Works: This Is England, sequel series\n- Topics: English independent film, skinhead subculture, far-right adoption, ska, soul, reggae\n\nFacts:\n- Shane Meadows was born on 26 December 1972 and is an English filmmaker of independent film.\n- In 2006, Shane Meadows wrote and directed the British drama film This Is England.\n- This Is England is set in England in 1983 and centres on young skinheads.\n- This Is England became one of Shane Meadows's best-known works, along with its three sequel series released from 2010 to 2015.\n- This Is England depicts the skinhead subculture's roots in 1960s West Indies culture, especially ska, soul, and reggae music.\n- This Is England shows how parts of the skinhead subculture were adopted by the far-right, especially white nationalists and white supremacists, causing divisions within the skinhead scene.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5f45a575-7627-5436-9ba1-0059ad548ce2",
        "text": "Page: Shane Meadows. Sentence: Shane Meadows (born 26 December 1972) is an English filmmaker of independent film.\nPage: Shane Meadows. Sentence: He is best known for the British cult film \"This Is England\" (2006) and \"its three sequel series\" (2010–2015).\nPage: This Is England. Sentence: This Is England is a 2006 British drama film written and directed by Shane Meadows.\nPage: This Is England. Sentence: The story centres on young skinheads in England in 1983.\nPage: This Is England. Sentence: The film illustrates how their subculture, which has its roots in 1960s West Indies culture, especially ska, soul, and reggae music, became adopted by the far-right, especially white nationalists and white supremacists, which led to divisions within the skinhead scene.",
